================================================================================
 - BACKEND ORM & DATABASE SCHEMA DOCUMENTATION
================================================================================

1. ARCHITECTURAL OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Medical Platform  database uses a normalized 1-to-1 relational design pattern:
- Base Identity Table (`users`): Manages credentials, authentication states, system roles, 
  and security control flags (brute-force defense and session versions).
- Domain Profile Tables (`patients`, `doctors`, `admins`): Hold role-specific clinical, 
  demographic, and administrative attributes linked via foreign keys to `users.user_id`.

2. MODEL SCHEMAS & RELATIONSHIPS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A. User Model (`users` table) - Defined in usr_orm.py
- user_id (Integer, Primary Key)
- username (String(150), Unique, Not Null)
- password_hash (String(255), Not Null) - Salted bcrypt hash
- role (String(20), Not Null) - ('PATIENT', 'DOCTOR', 'ADMIN')
- is_locked (Boolean, Default: False) - Brute-force lockout flag
- failed_attempts (Integer, Default: 0) - Consecutive invalid login counter
- token_version (Integer, Default: 1) - Incremented to invalidate all active JWT sessions
- created_at (DateTime with Timezone)
- Relationships: 1-to-1 cascading deletes with Patient, Doctor, and Admin models.

B. Patient Profile Model (`patients` table) - Defined in pat_orm.py
- patient_id (Integer, Primary Key)
- user_id (Integer, Foreign Key -> users.user_id, Unique, Cascade Delete)
- Demographics: first_name, middle_name, last_name, suffix, date_of_birth, gender, religion
- Contact & Emergency: address, contact_number, email, emergency_contact_name, 
  emergency_contact_number, emergency_relation
- Compliance: hipaa_consent (Boolean), hipaa_consent_at, is_active (Boolean)

C. Doctor Profile Model (`doctors` table) - Defined in doc_orm.py
- doctor_id (Integer, Primary Key)
- user_id (Integer, Foreign Key -> users.user_id, Unique, Cascade Delete)
- Demographics & Credentials: first_name, middle_name, last_name, suffix, license_number (Unique)
- Professional: specialization, hospital_affiliation
- Contact & Emergency: address, contact_number, email, emergency_contact_name, 
  emergency_contact_number, emergency_relation
- Verification: is_verified (Boolean)

D. Admin Profile Model (`admins` table) - Defined in adm_orm.py
- admin_id (Integer, Primary Key)
- user_id (Integer, Foreign Key -> users.user_id, Unique, Cascade Delete)
- Demographics & Credentials: first_name, middle_name, last_name, suffix, license_number (Unique)
- Organizational: specialization, hospital_affiliation
- Contact & Emergency: address, contact_number, email, emergency_contact_name, 
  emergency_contact_number, emergency_relation
- Verification: is_verified (Boolean)